SELECT define_rule($q${"rule_id": "TCC.tcc_cr_buildings_front_setback_average", "instrument_version": "TCC_CITY_PLAN_2014@2025-12-08", "topic": "SETBACK.FRONTAGE", "title": "Table 6.2.5.3 PO14 / AO14.1", "role": "REQUIREMENT", "regime": "BUILDING", "enforceability": "DEEMED_TO_COMPLY", "provision_kind": "ACCEPTABLE_OUTCOME", "measurement": "SCHEME_SETBACK_FRONT", "operator": ">=", "value": {"op": "unencoded", "text": "0.9 * avg_adjoining_contributing_front_setback <= setback <= 1.1 * avg_adjoining_contributing_front_setback", "extracted_value": null, "extracted_operator": "conditional"}, "unit": "m", "on_noncompliance": "REFERRAL_TO_LOCAL_GOVERNMENT", "effective_from": "2025-12-08", "verification": "VERIFIED_VERBATIM", "automatable": false, "scopes": [{"level": "LOCAL_GOVERNMENT", "lg": "TOWNSVILLE"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "TCC:CHARACTER_RESIDENTIAL"}], "subjects": ["ANY"], "sources": [{"key": "tcc_cr_buildings_front_setback_average", "role": "PRIMARY"}], "interpretation_notes": "AUTO-IMPORTED (draft). Extracted structure: {\"parameter\": \"street_setback_relative_to_adjoining_average\", \"operator\": \"conditional\", \"value\": null, \"unit\": \"m\", \"conditions\": [\"assessable development only\", \"within 10% of the average front setback of adjoining contributing character buildings\"], \"exceptions\": [], \"formula_text\": \"0.9 * avg_adjoining_contributing_front_setback <= setback <= 1.1 * avg_adjoining_contributing_front_setback\"}\nStructure scope 'Buildings and extensions (new building, relocation of a contributing character building within the site or extension or alteration to an existing contributing character building)' mapped by keyword to ['ANY'] (default)\nAlternative provision to QDC/QHC: YES - Table 6.2.5.3 editor’s note: \"This code contains alternative provisions for dwelling houses and dual occupancies to those set out in the Queensland Development Code (MP 1.1, MP 1.2 and MP 1.3), for the purposes of section 33 of the Building Act 1975.\"; Part 1 Table 1.6.1 lists the Character Residential Zone as \"Building assessment provisions – regulated building work in accordance with sections 32 and 33 of the Building Act 1975\"\nResearcher notes: Scope ambiguity: \"Buildings\" is not limited to the dwelling, so a new class 10a building made assessable by Table 5.7.1 may be caught; but the more specific AO9(a) governs carports/garages. Curator to decide whether to apply to Class 10."}$q$::jsonb);
